summary: R22.43 names resolved through hosted/blocking by a static Linux program's hosts file and resolv.conf and elsewhere the C library's or Windows' resolver: an address's text is itself, localhost gives 127.0.0.1 with the port, connect_by_name reaches a listener on 127.0.0.1 alone, a .invalid name is unknown_name or timed_out where no server can be reached, a name too long is unknown_name, and net.ask of a server that never answers is timed_out
